//File:    jac313_connections.jtext
//Purpose: PostgreSQL servers for jac313 test runs (pg-local / pg-remote).
//         EXAMPLE ONLY (docs/SQL_Secrets_example). The real file lives in a SQL_Secrets folder
//         beside the project, e.g. ~/git/SQL_Secrets/, never inside a git project.
//         No passwords here: they are in jac313_pg_local.pgpass / jac313_pg_remote.pgpass.
//
=== jText File ===
 1. #?# jac313_connections
 3. #?# PostgreSQL connections for jac313 / Jac313Runner


=== Section: connections ===


=== Fields ===
 1. #/# id/Identity(1,1)/Not Null     # record id
 2. #/# backend/String/Not Null       # pg-local | pg-remote
 3. #/# host/String/Not Null          # host name or IP address
 4. #/# port/Number                   # 5432 is PostgreSQL's usual port
 5. #/# dbname/String
 6. #/# user/String
 7. #/# connect_timeout/Number        # seconds
 8. #/# notes/String
=== End Fields ===


=== Data ===
1. #|# 1|pg-local|localhost|5432|jac313|jac313|10|this machine (bootstrap sets it up)

1. #|# 2|pg-remote|db.example.org|5432|jac313|jac313|10|your own server

=== End Data ===
=== End Section ===
=== End File ===
